        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "So then if, while her husband liveth, she be married to another man, she shall be called an adulteress: but if her husband be dead, she is free from that law; so that she is no adulteress, though she be married to another man.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 7:3",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore, my brethren, ye also are become dead to the law by the body of Christ; that ye should be married to another, even to him who is raised from the dead, that we should bring forth fruit unto God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "Gal. 2:19; 2 Ne. 25:25 (24–27); D&C 74:5 (2–6)."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "Mosiah 13:28 (27–29)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 124
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 7:4",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "For when we were in the flesh, the motions of sins, which were by the law, did work in our members to bring forth fruit unto death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "JST Rom. 7:5–27 (Appendix)."
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "GR sufferings, afflictions."
          },
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "2 Ne. 2:5 (4–10); 25:23; Alma 42:14 (12–16)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Romans 7:5",
        "book": "Romans",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "But now we are delivered from the law, that being dead wherein we were held; that we should serve in newness of spirit, and not in the oldness of the letter.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "GR released, freed from."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "2 Cor. 5:17."
          },
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 118,
            "text": "Rom. 2:29 (28–29)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 130
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
